<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Israel</h1><p class="st-meta">1948 CE – present · capital Jerusalem</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Jewish state declared in 1948 at the end of the British mandate, built through war, mass immigration and a long unresolved conflict.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Zionist settlement under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mandatory-palestine">Mandatory Palestine</a> built the institutions of a state in waiting. After the United Nations voted to partition Palestine in 1947, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-ben-gurion">David Ben-Gurion</a> declared independence on 14 May 1948; the war that followed secured the new state against the armies of its neighbours, while some 700,000 Palestinian Arabs fled or were driven from their homes, remembered as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakba">Nakba</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A parliamentary republic governed from the Knesset, with Jerusalem as its seat of government, though recognition of the city as capital remains disputed. Mass immigration gathered Jews from Europe, the Middle East and North Africa; Hebrew was revived as a language of daily life; and a conscript army fought the wars of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/six-day-war">1967</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yom-kippur-war">1973</a> that reshaped the region's borders and politics.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Peace treaties with Egypt in 1979 and Jordan in 1994 ended the state of war with two neighbours, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo-accords">Oslo Accords</a> of 1993-1995 began, then stalled, a peace process with the Palestinians. A technology-driven economy and the continuing occupation of territories captured in 1967 define Israel's contested present.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1948 CE – present"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-